<section class="differentiator">
  <div class="diff-inner">
    <div class="diff-label">Why the industry hasn't solved this yet</div>
    <h2 class="diff-headline">Healthcare built systems to find sick patients. Nobody built systems to find recovering ones.</h2>
    <div class="diff-grid">
      <div class="diff-col">
        <div class="diff-col-label">The old approach</div>
        <ul class="diff-list diff-list--old">
          <li>Predict when patients get <em>worse</em></li>
          <li>Point solutions for one problem at a time</li>
          <li>Device manufacturers see vital signs only</li>
          <li>Black-box AI — no clinical trust</li>
          <li>Siloed data, no unified signal layer</li>
          <li>Reactive alerts that add to the noise</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <div class="diff-col">
        <div class="diff-col-label">AlertPulse approach</div>
        <ul class="diff-list diff-list--new">
          <li>Predict both deterioration <em>and</em> recovery</li>
          <li>Platform — one data layer, many use cases</li>
          <li>Fuses Epic + Philips + GE + meds + history</li>
          <li>Transparent AI — every recommendation explained</li>
          <li>Unified signal format built for data science</li>
          <li>Autonomous triage agents act, not just alert</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>